{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJpcm8S36gH49FH3ZTgx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed the `FILE_UPLOAD_PERMISSIONS` default from `None` to `0o644`, so uploaded files get the same mode whether they were small (in memory) or large (temp file). `test_utils.tests` now has one failure, which I left alone because the rules say not to edit tests.\n\n- **Reproduction:** the default read back as `None`.\n- **Root cause:** `django/conf/global_settings.py` set the default to `None`, so the saved file's mode depended on which upload handler ran. A temp-file upload kept `0o600` and an in-memory one used the umask.\n- **Fix:** the default is now `0o644` in `django/conf/global_settings.py`. I also updated the setting's entry in `docs/ref/settings.txt` to show the new default and describe `None` as the OS-dependent option.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **`test_utils.tests`:** one failure, `test_override_file_upload_permissions`. It asserts `assertIsNone(default_storage.file_permissions_mode)`, which encodes the old `None` default, so it now gets `420` (`0o644`). That assertion needs updating to match the new default.\n- **`file_storage`:** `FileLikeObjectTestCase.setUpClass` raises `PermissionError`. It fails the same way with my changes stashed, so it isn't caused by this fix.\n\nI didn't add a release note."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":22144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":575},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6dbd07b-2aec-4e47-9ecf-32109227eca4","uuid":"0c02a98e-9869-4e23-9ff3-7494cd2eec3e","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:18:56.337Z","request_id":"req_011ChJpckyFhN